name o5-09-night-two-1
timeout 900
time 1999-03-25T21:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O5, SORTIE 9 OF 10 - AIRFIELD DEFENCE: BATAJNICA, 24-26 MARCH 1999.
# CHAIN - THE NIGHT OF 25/26 MARCH 1999, WITH THE MISSILES RELEASED.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - chain step 2 of 3. Its predecessor is o5-08-night-one.fbm.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. Batajnica lies at ~44.93 N 20.26 E [T4, approximate -
# doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md says so and this campaign does not improve on it]. FlightBox flies
# it under `--elev const` on a 0 m datum (the real field is ~80 m) and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4),
# so the Fruska Gora, the Danube valley and every mask a Serbian battery used do not exist here. The
# field's runway heading (110 deg) and length (3 000 m) are [SET]; nothing in this campaign lands.
#   the field       44.93000 20.26000, with the fuel farm, a hangar row, one hardened shelter and the
#                   runway aim point around it
#   the point defence  P-18 node at 20.24000 (on the field), S-125 at 20.16000 (7.9 km W), 2K12 at
#                   20.19000/44.95500 (5.7 km W, 2.8 km N), ZSU-23-4 at 20.25200 (0.7 km W)
#   the package     ingresses due east along 44.93 N from 19.60000 (52.0 km out) at 5 000 m and 450 kt
# Scale at this latitude: 1 deg of longitude = 78 800 m, 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION. The package that attacked Batajnica was F-15C, F-117 and cruise
# missiles [T4]; FlightBox flies F-16s for all three, which is declared and not hidden. THE F-15C ROW
# EXISTS AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED, and the reason was MEASURED in this round rather than assumed:
# `modules/air/FBAirModule` composes NO FIRE CONTROL, so `FBState::FireControl` is never written and all
# three of FBPilot's weapon-employment gates stay shut. Measured: an `f15c` with four AIM-120 designates
# at t = 8.6 s at 18.64 nm, holds `eng_locked = 1` for 28 s from 18.6 down to 8.8 nm, and never posts a
# WeaponRelease. A catalogue row is ACCEPTED as a FLIGHT MODEL, not as a combatant.
# The defender is the MiG-29 the 127th "Knights" actually flew - so unlike O1 and O3 the substitution
# here is on the ATTACKER's side, and it makes the attacker WEAKER than history (no F-117, no cruise
# missile, no AIM-7/AMRAAM mix from a 160 km radar). A FlightBox Batajnica in which the field still
# loses says something WEAKER than 1999 did, not stronger.
#
# THE TWO LAYERS CANNOT BOTH BE LIVE, AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURE - stated in every
# file because a reader who skips it will read every result backwards.
#   1. A FlightBox SAM site has NO IFF INTERROGATOR (`modules/ground/FBSiteModule`: "a battery has no
#      IFF interrogator in this tree") and an FBRadarContact carries no identity by construction, so a
#      battery engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK in its envelope whoever it belongs to. An AIRFIELD is
#      exactly the geometry in which the friendly aircraft are the nearest track: O1 could lay its CAP
#      outside its own umbrella, O5 cannot, because the defenders live under it.
#   2. `missions/FBMissionRunner` ENDS THE WHOLE RUN at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`),
#      and a mission-killed F-16 falls from 5 000 m in about 122 s. So an air engagement and a bomb run
#      in one file are not two measurements, they are one measurement and a truncation.
# The answer taken is the one a real airfield takes and the only one this format can express: the
# missiles are HELD while the fighters are up (`set emcon hold <offS> <onS>`, the briefed emission plan
# of round C26) and free when they are not. Sorties 01-05 therefore measure the FIGHTER layer with the
# belt briefed quiet; 06-07 measure the MISSILE layer with no fighter airborne; the chain 08-10 lets the
# campaign's own attrition decide which layer is left. THE CAMPAIGN NEVER MEASURES BOTH AT ONCE, and any
# claim that it did would be manufactured.
#
# WHAT CARRIES, AND IT IS THE CAMPAIGN'S SUBJECT. `carry units ground stores`, not narrowed - a defender
# that loses aircraft defends worse the next night, and that sentence is the whole reason this chain
# exists. Three nights share ONE defending roster (`knight1`..`knight5`) and ONE set of ground callsigns
# (`bat*`), so every MiG killed and every position destroyed is DROPPED from the next file by the
# campaign overlay, and every `set store` line spent is dropped from the next spawn.
# THE ATTACKER DOES NOT CARRY, and that is a declaration rather than an omission: each night's package
# has its own callsigns (`n1*`, `n2*`, `n3*`), because NATO flew ~38 000 sorties over 78 days against a
# squadron that had a dozen airframes, and a campaign layer that attrited both sides equally would be
# modelling a war that did not happen. The asymmetry is in the CALLSIGNS, where a reader can see it.
# WHAT DOES NOT CARRY AND SHOULD: a battery's expended rounds. `set rounds` is not `set store`, and the
# campaign layer's store carry is keyed on `set store` lines (doc/missions/campaign.md section 4), so a
# battery that shot itself dry is full again the next night. Gap, named here, inherited from O1.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: THE MISSILES ARE RELEASED AND OUR OWN FIGHTERS ARE STILL UP. WHO DOES THE
# BELT SHOOT? `set emcon hold 1 3600` is gone from the three fire units - one changed value per position,
# nothing else - so tonight the field defends itself while whatever survived sortie 08 is airborne over
# it. A FlightBox battery has no IFF interrogator and engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK; the defenders orbit
# at 9 000 m, 20.6 km east of the S-125, and the package arrives from 52 km west. The arithmetic is in
# the file and the answer is in `site LAUNCH ... brgDeg`.
#
# THIS IS NOT A CONTROLLED VARIANT OF 08 and must not be read as one - it is the next step of the chain,
# so it differs from 08 in the emission plan AND in everything the carry took away. The campaign layer's
# own rule (doc/missions/campaign.md Gaps): a chain step cannot also be a control.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 4db885e9157b58c3, AS CAMPAIGN STEP 9): THE MISSILES WERE RELEASED AND THERE WERE
# NO MISSILES LEFT TO RELEASE. The carry drops `batnod` and `batsa3` (destroyed on night one), so the
# surviving 2K12 has no node: `net WCS unit=batsa6 state=hold netState=SILENT correlated=0
# effect="launch inhibited" rangeM=6591.55` at t = 33.0 - IT HOLDS A FIRM TRACK ON ONE OF ITS OWN
# FIGHTERS AT 6.6 km AND THE MISSING NODE IS WHAT STOPS IT FIRING. Zero launches. `knight1` is lost to an
# AIM-120, and six `set store` lines were dropped from the pair's racks before it took off.
# STANDALONE, WITH THE NODE ALIVE, THE SAME FILE ANSWERS THE QUESTION IT WAS WRITTEN FOR: seven launches,
# and THE FIRST THREE GO EAST AT THE FIELD'S OWN MiG-29s (`brgDeg` 116.5 / 90.6 / 91.0, at 6.5 / 7.0 /
# 6.6 km) before four go west at the package (258.6 / 271.5 / 272.4 / 258.8). A FlightBox battery has no
# IFF interrogator and an airfield is the one geometry in which that cannot be laid around. The campaign
# is what prevented the fratricide, by destroying the node that would have authorised it.
#
# READING RULE: any exit. Read `site LAUNCH` with `brgDeg` FIRST - a bearing near 270 is the package, a
# bearing near 090 is our own pair - then the DETONATION lines with `target=`, then the bombs. The number
# this sortie exists to produce is "rounds spent on friendly aircraft", and it is a count of log lines.

zone umbrella 44.93000 20.16000 35000 100 18000   # the S-125's published envelope, as geometry
zone field    44.93000 20.26000  6000   0  6000   # the terminal box: first entry is the time-on-target

net batajnica
  control batnod
  link radio 60000 mast 8
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member batnod
  member batsa3 autonomy hold
  member batsa6 autonomy hold
  member batflk autonomy hold

unit knight1
  team hostile
  flight kn1 1
  module mig29
  spawn 44.93000 20.35000 6000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r73
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 50 5
  set brief_gci 60 270 31 5
  set brief_gci 100 270 13 5
  wp 44.93000 19.40000 6000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective deny release team friendly
  objective survive

